            0.305
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "6.3.4 What is soluble in water; what is not?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.311,
            0.324,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.341,
            0.317,
            0.884,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": "Ghulan was sweating when he came home after playing in the evening. He was feeling tired and thirsty. Ghulan’s mother mixed a spoonful of sugar, a pinch of salt and some lemon juice in a glass tumbler of water and offered him this shikanji (lemonade) to drink."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.342,
            0.439,
            0.883,
            0.501
          ],
          "content": "Ghulan noticed that while his mother was mixing sugar and salt in water, the salt and the sugar disappeared after a while."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.342,
            0.501,
            0.883,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": "Let us try a simple activity to explore how different materials behave when we mix them in water!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.579,
            0.545,
            0.601
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 6.7: Let us explore"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.617,
            0.883,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "Collect small amounts of sugar, salt, chalk powder, sand and sawdust."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.664,
            0.882,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": "Take five glass tumblers and fill them about two-third with water."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.711,
            0.883,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": " Put a teaspoonful of sugar in the first glass tumbler, salt in the second one, chalk powder in the third, sand in the fourth and sawdust in the fifth glass tumbler."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.775,
            0.837,
            0.797
          ],
          "content": " On stirring, **predict** what will happen in each case."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.8,
            0.882,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": " Use a spoon to stir well the contents of each glass tumbler."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.827,
            0.818,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": "Wait for a few minutes and watch what happens."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.853,
            0.757,
            0.874
          ],
          "content": " Write down your observations in Table 6.5."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
